<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramon Llull</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1232–1316</span> · Also known as Raymond Lull</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramon Llull was a philosopher, mystic and missionary from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a>, born soon after the Aragonese conquest of the island. He wrote over 200 works in Catalan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and Arabic, including the novel Blanquerna and the Ars Magna, a method for proving Christian truths to Muslims and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. He is considered one of the founders of Catalan literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramon-llull.jpg" alt="Ramon Llull" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesc Ribalta · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francisco_Ribalta_-_Ramon_Llull_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
